# Project-Specific Rules (vx-binocle-espidf)

## 6. Non-Factory Screen File Parity Across `main/` Directory
- **Strict 100% File Parity**: ALL files inside the `main/` subfolder across `left_screen` and `right_screen` (`main.cpp`, `twai_ops.hpp`, `start_animation.hpp`, `global_vars.hpp`, `updateUI.hpp`, `CMakeLists.txt`, `idf_component.yml`, `Kconfig.projbuild`, etc.) MUST maintain 100% byte-for-byte content parity (`diff -r left_screen/main right_screen/main` must return 0 diffs).
- **Macro-Based Differentiation**: Differentiate screen-specific behavior strictly using compile-time macro switches (e.g. `CONFIG_LEFT_SIDE_DISPLAY` / `#ifdef CONFIG_LEFT_SIDE_DISPLAY` / `#else`) rather than maintaining separate divergent source files.
- **Component Exemption**: This core parity rule does NOT apply to generated UI components (e.g. `components/ui` or EEZ Studio generated code), which are allowed to differ per screen.

## 7. Shared Component Integrity & TWAI API Standards
- **No Direct Edits to Shared/Managed Components**: Do not edit `common/twai_daemon`, `common/binocan`, or `common/lvgl_v9_port` directly inside `managed_components` or shared folders when resolving application issues.
- **Clean TWAI Integration**: In `left_screen` and `right_screen`, send CAN messages directly via `twai_daemon_transmit(&tx_msg, ticks)`. Avoid legacy task handles (`CAN_RX_tsk_hdl`, `CAN_TX_tsk_hdl`) and FreeRTOS macro overloads (`#define vTaskSuspend ...`), using standard `TaskHandle_t CAN_Dispatch_Task_hdl` for task pause/resume.

## 8. Global README Sub-Project External Dependency Matrix
- **Dependency Summary Table**: The top-level repository `README.md` MUST contain and maintain a structured summary table of external dependencies across all sub-projects (e.g., `left_screen`, `right_screen`, `interface_board`, `emulator-console`, `factory apps`, etc.).
- **Required Columns**:
  - **Sub-Project**: Name of the sub-project directory.
  - **External Dependency**: Name of the component package invoked via `idf_component.yml`.
  - **Locally Installed Version**: Exact version tag or short git commit SHA currently installed in `managed_components` / `dependencies.lock`.
  - **Version Requirement**: The constraint or version specification declared in `idf_component.yml` (when available).

## 9. Sub-Project Documentation Standards (`README.md` & `TOO.MD`)
- **Sub-Project `README.md` Content**: `README.md` files located at the root of individual sub-projects (`interface_board`, `left_screen`, `right_screen`, `factory apps/*`) MUST remain lightweight, technical, and human-focused. They should describe subproject purpose, target SoC, display/network configuration, and key firmware capabilities.
- **Exclusion of Agent Instructions**: Sub-project `README.md` files MUST NOT contain agentic prompt instructions, internal rule citations (e.g. "Rule 6"), or AI operational constraint references. Agent-specific guidelines belong in repo-level files (`REQUIREMENTS.md`, `README.md`, or `.geminirules`).
- **Theory of Operation (`TOO.MD`) Requirement**: Each active sub-project and major shared component (`common/twai_daemon`) MUST maintain a `TOO.MD` (or `OTA_TOO.MD`) detailing system architecture, hardware subsystems, signal processing, CAN ingestion/dispatch loops, API endpoints, and sequence diagrams (including protocol handshakes and timeout/error escape points).

## 10. Portable Relative Markdown Links
- **Relative Path Invariant**: All file references inside repository Markdown (`.md`) files MUST use relative file paths (e.g., `[TOO.MD](TOO.MD)` or `[main/main.cpp](main/main.cpp)`).
- **No Absolute Filesystem URLs**: NEVER commit absolute local filesystem URLs (e.g. `file:///home/user/...`) inside repository documentation to preserve author privacy and ensure links render correctly on GitHub.


